  "body": {
    "id": "prop:fixed-horizon-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "When \\(K=1\\), \\(\\mathcal K_n=\\{0\\}\\), the eligible set contains one target block \\(E_0=\\{g_0\\}\\), and \\(\\widehat\\Omega_{00}>0\\), \\(c_{0q}\\) and \\(\\Omega_{00}\\) reduce to the Choi--Yuan Proposition A.4 influence coefficients and their heteroskedastic scalar influence variance, while \\(\\widehat\\Omega_{00}\\) and \\(\\mathcal C_{n,0}\\) reduce to the Choi--Kwon--Liao-style unit-residual plug-in variance and the ordinary studentized scalar interval.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "K",
      "Kn",
      "E",
      "c",
      "Omega",
      "hatOmega",
      "Band",
      "n",
      "q"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:staircase-influence-map",
      "def:heteroskedastic-plugin",
      "def:multiplier-band",
      "ass:row-heteroskedasticity"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Under the proposed positivity qualification, let \\(E_0=\\{g_0\\}\\).\nThen \\(N_0=n_{g_0}\\), so the outer weight \\(n_{g_0}/N_0\\) in the\ndefinition of \\(c_{0q}\\) equals one.  The displayed formula for\n\\(c_{0,(u,v)}\\) consequently becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathbf 1\\{u\\in I_{g_0},\\ v=g_0\\}}{n_{g_0}}\n-\\mathbf 1\\{u\\in J_{g_0,0},\\ v=g_0\\}\n \\bar x_{g_0}^{\\top}A_{g_0,0}^{-1}x_u\n-\\frac{\\mathbf 1\\{u\\in I_{g_0},\\ v\\in S_{g_0}\\}}{n_{g_0}}\n z_{g_0}^{\\top}B_{g_0}^{-1}z_v,\n\\]\nwhich is exactly the single-block coefficient to which\n\\(\\texttt{def:staircase-influence-map}\\) refers.  With only one\ncoordinate, the covariance and its feasible counterpart are, directly\nfrom their definitions,\n\\[\n\\Omega_{00}=\\sum_{q=(u,v)\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}\nc_{0q}^2\\sigma_{uv}^2,\n\\qquad\n\\widehat\\Omega_{00}=\\sum_{q=(u,v)\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}\n\\widehat c_{0q}^{,2}\\widehat\\sigma_u^2.\n\\]\nAssumption \\(\\texttt{ass:row-heteroskedasticity}\\), which is a member\nproperty of the class used by the plug-in construction, changes the\nfirst display's variance to \\(\\sigma_u^2\\); the second display is thus\nthe corresponding unit-residual plug-in form.\n\nIt remains to check the scalar critical value.  The proposed condition\n\\(\\widehat\\Omega_{00}>0\\) implies\n\\(\\widehat s_0=\\sqrt{\\widehat\\Omega_{00}}>0\\), so the division in the\nmultiplier statistic is defined.  Conditional on \\(Y\\), independence\nand normality of the multipliers give\n\\[\n\\widetilde Z\n=\\sum_{q=(u,v)\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}\n  \\frac{\\widehat c_{0q}\\widehat\\sigma_u}{\\widehat s_0}\\xi_q\n\\sim N\\!\\left(0,\n\\frac{\\sum_q\\widehat c_{0q}^{,2}\\widehat\\sigma_u^2}\n     {\\widehat s_0^2}\\right)\n=N(0,1).\n\\]\nThus \\(W_n^\\xi=|\\widetilde Z|\\), its conditional \\((1-\\alpha)\\)-quantile\nis the ordinary two-sided standard-normal critical value, and\n\\(\\mathcal C_{n,0}=[\\widehat\\tau_0\\pm\nc_{1-\\alpha,n}\\widehat s_0]\\) is the ordinary studentized scalar\ninterval.  Every reduction is algebraic; no growing-dimensional limit\ntheorem is used.",
